---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="How it works — Running Stats"
  description="A coach AI that answers what to run today and adapts the plan when you miss a session or life changes."
  heading="How it works"
>
  <p>
    Running Stats is a coach AI for one question: what should you run today? It
    is not a generic tracker of distance, pace, and badges.
  </p>
  <p>
    You bring a goal and the realities of your week. Each day you get a clear
    session—or rest—instead of a static calendar that ignores missed runs.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you skip, cut short, or feel off, the plan adapts. The next "today"
    session is rebuilt around what actually happened, not what was written on
    Monday.
  </p>
  <p>
    Detail views for today's session, the full plan, and progress land in a later
    pass. This page is the product explanation, not those screens.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a
      href="/start"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-lime px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase shadow-[0_8px_28px_rgba(184,245,44,0.2)] transition-[background-color,transform,box-shadow] duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-[#cbff50]"
    >
      Start your plan
    </a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
